# Flowchart explanations

When explaining how the site, APIs, build, or deploy work, always use a **Mermaid flowchart** (not ASCII `↓` / `→` text trees).

Prefer this style:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  srcHtml["src/pages/*.html"] --> vite[Vite build]
  srcJs["src/js/site.js + modules"] --> vite
  srcScss["src/styles/*.scss"] --> vite
  srcPartials["src/partials/*.hbs"] --> vite
  vite --> dist["dist/ HTML + hashed CSS/JS"]
  dist --> s3cf[S3 + CloudFront]
  s3cf --> live["https://khansaiful.com"]
```

Guidelines:
- Use `flowchart TD` (top-down) or `flowchart LR` (left-right)
- Name real files, services, and endpoints from this project
- Keep a short prose summary, then the flowchart as the main explanation
- In Markdown files use fenced `mermaid` blocks
- In HTML pages use `<pre class="mermaid">...</pre>` (rendered by site.js)
